  <!-- SECTION 7: FAQS & GUIDELINES -->
  <section id="hilo-faqs" aria-labelledby="hilo-faqs-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="hilo-faqs-title">FAQs</h2></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-panel">
<div class="hilo-faq-list">
      <details class="hilo-faq-item">
        <summary><h3>How do I obtain physical seed stocks for the HiLo landraces and inbreds?</h3></summary>
        <div class="hilo-faq-body">
          <p>
            Seed stocks for the traditional landraces are preserved in national and international germplasm repositories:
            Palomero de Jalisco \(<a href="https://npgsweb.ars-grin.gov/gringlobal/accessiondetail?id=1925923" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PI 693885</a>\),
            Tabloncillo \(<a href="https://npgsweb.ars-grin.gov/gringlobal/accessiondetail?id=1925925" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ames 32914</a>\),
            Zapalote Chico \(<a href="https://npgsweb.ars-grin.gov/gringlobal/accessiondetail?id=1842814" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ames 30536</a>\),
            and CIMMYT inbreds through the <a href="https://www.cimmyt.org/resources/seed-request/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CIMMYT Germplasm Bank</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="hilo-faq-item">
        <summary><h3>Where can I download the complete FASTA sequences and GFF3 gene annotations?</h3></summary>
        <div class="hilo-faq-body">
          <p>
            All assemblies, GFF3 annotation files, and predicted CDS/peptide FASTA sequences can be downloaded directly from the <a href="/download#downloads-hilo">MaizeGDB Downloads Portal</a> or via individual assembly links in the table above.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="hilo-faq-item">
        <summary><h3>How should I cite the HiLo project in research publications?</h3></summary>
        <div class="hilo-faq-body">
          <p>
            Please cite <strong>Perez-Lim&oacute;n et al. \(2022\)</strong>, <em>A B73 &times; Palomero Toluque&ntilde;o mapping population reveals local adaptation in Mexican highland maize</em>, G3&#58; Genes, Genomes, Genetics 12\(2\)&#58;jkab447 \(<a href="https://doi.org/10.1093/g3journal/jkab447" target="_blank" rel="noopener">doi&#58;10.1093/g3journal/jkab447</a>\), along with NSF Award #1546719 and the MaizeGDB database citation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="hilo-faq-item">
        <summary><h3>Can I compare HiLo genomes with B73 in JBrowse 2?</h3></summary>
        <div class="hilo-faq-body">
          <p>
            Yes! Launch <a href="/genomebrowser">JBrowse 2</a>, select any HiLo assembly, and use the Track Selector to add synteny, gene models, and comparative alignments against B73 RefGen_v5.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>

  </section>

